// Rule: [T1490] Gunra - WMIC Shadowcopy Deletion
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1490
// Classification: Production candidate
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Behavioral candidate for source-observed volume shadow-copy deletion through WMIC before ransomware impact.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for wmic shadowcopy deletion using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: An endpoint invoked the complete WMIC shadow-copy deletion pattern and requires urgent validation of authorization, execution result and surrounding impact.
// A match does not prove: Successful deletion, loss of backups, file encryption, data theft, malicious intent or Gunra attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Gunra / WMIC shadow-copy deletion
// Classification: Production candidate - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint process creation events
// Source evidence: AA26-222A documents the exact WMIC shadowcopy delete behavior.
// No threshold, rarity, join, sequence, hash, domain, or campaign attribution is used.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName =~ "WMIC.exe"
| where ProcessCommandLine has "shadowcopy"
| where ProcessCommandLine has "delete"
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceId,
    DeviceName,
    AccountName,
    AccountUpn,
    FileName,
    FolderPath,
    ProcessCommandLine,
    ProcessId,
    ProcessUniqueId,
    ProcessIntegrityLevel,
    ProcessTokenElevation,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessAccountName,
    InitiatingProcessAccountUpn,
    IsProcessRemoteSession,
    ProcessRemoteSessionIP,
    SHA1,
    InitiatingProcessSHA1,
    ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
